#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD9729 expect=noViolation domain=TE
#note "Both columns are present (blank on row 2), so both var_exists leaves are false and the sister stays silent - the record-level pair check is the parent FDA-SD0089's job. Together with -violation_no_columns and -noViolation_only_teenrl_column this pins the sister to EXACTLY the neither-column state."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset TE label="Trial Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col ELEMENT type=Char label="Description of Element"
col TESTRL  type=Char label="Rule for Start of Element"
col TEENRL  type=Char label="Rule for End of Element"
col TEDUR   type=Char label="Planned Duration of Element"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TE | SCRN | Screening | Informed consent | End of screening | P14D
CDISCPILOT01 | TE | TRT | Treatment | First dose |  |
